# Digital forensics — spec section 14.
# Spec requires clearly marking read-only vs data-modifying operations
# (section 14 closing note) — that's a Tool Launcher / Security Center UI
# responsibility, not something a package list can express, but flagging
# here so it isn't lost: sleuthkit/autopsy operations are read-only against
# a disk image by design; ddrescue and dc3dd are NOT (they write copies).

sleuthkit
autopsy
testdisk
foremost
binwalk
exiftool
dc3dd

# gddrescue is the Debian package name — it PROVIDES the `ddrescue`
# command; Debian's actual `ddrescue` package (no g-prefix) is a
# different, older, unrelated tool. bulk-extractor and theharvester are
# not Debian packages at all (Kali-only apt package, in bulk-extractor's
# case, and source/pip-only for theharvester) — moved to
# 0300-raptor-thirdparty-tools.hook.chroot's best-effort installer
# instead of left here as a build-breaking entry.
gddrescue
